// Feature: the campaign's life. Code: lib/campaign-flow.ts (pure stages), muster.ts, rounds.ts, games.ts, campaign.ts.
views {
  dynamic view campaign_flow {
    title 'Campaign flow'
    description '''
      **From founding to the final reckoning.** Stages run setup → mustering → underway →
      ended (`campaign-flow.ts`, shared by server and pages).

      **Decisions**
      - Seats come first: the CM sizes the campaign, each seat gets an invite link (single use,
        seven days), and joining makes the account and seats it.
      - A campaign needs at least two warbands to get under way; the CM can override other
        mustering checks.
      - Rounds of battles: players roll for Aggressor, Aggressors pick opponents and battlefields,
        battles roll Hell on Earth. Each step holds a Postgres advisory lock, so a double tap or
        a player and the CM at once can't act twice.
      - The campaign state is replayed from its events (games and adjustments) by the pure rules
        engine, on the server and in the browser alike.
    '''
    cm -> cf.app.web.admin 'found the campaign, set the seats'
    cf.app.web.admin -> cf.app.server.campaign 'ensureSeats, issueInvite'
    player -> cf.app.web.door 'follow the invite link'
    cf.app.web.door -> cf.app.server.campaign 'redeemInvite: account + seat'
    player -> cf.app.web.public 'muster: found the warband, pick a Vision'
    cm -> cf.app.web.admin 'advance to under way'
    player -> cf.app.web.public 'the round: roll, pick an opponent and a field'
    cf.app.web.public -> cf.app.web.api '/api/round'
    cf.app.web.api -> cf.app.server.campaign 'one locked step at a time (rounds.ts)'
    cm -> cf.app.web.admin 'record the battle'
    cf.app.web.admin -> cf.app.server.campaign 'commitGame, closeRoundIfDone'
    cf.app.server.campaign -> cf.app.ui.engine 'replay the events: standings'
  }
}
